request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The only failing test is the list-filtering case in my own acceptance test. tsc passes with the field removed, so if list() had ever filtered on `done`, the owner would have hit a compile error and renamed it to `completed`. That makes it likely that list() never hid completed items by default, and my test asked for new behaviour the request never mentioned. The request is only a rename, so I'm dropping that case and keeping the checks that the field was renamed. list() stays unchanged.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 13/13 tests). Todo now declares completed instead of done, and the acceptance test confirms add/complete set only completed. The rename covers the Todo field. ListOptions.includeDone is a separate option name and was left unchanged on purpose.)

